    <fr:title text="Example: Current vs. Rich Rendering">Example: Current vs. Rich Rendering</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Referenced from <fr:link href="/sss-008X/" title="Rich Forest Rendering in Emacs" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-008X/" display-uri="sss-008X" type="local">Rich Forest Rendering in Emacs</fr:link>. Shows concrete examples of Forester markup that renders well in a browser but degrades to plain text in the current Emacs preview.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Inline math.</html:strong> Source: <html:code><![CDATA[#{e^{i \pi} + 1 = 0}]]></html:code>. In-browser: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[e^{i \pi } + 1 = 0]]></fr:tex>. In current Emacs preview: the raw source, with no KaTeX rendering.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Display math.</html:strong> Source: <html:code><![CDATA[##{\sum_{n=0}^{\infty} \frac{1}{n!} = e}]]></html:code>. In-browser:</html:p>
    <fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\sum _{n=0}^{\infty } \frac {1}{n!} = e]]></fr:tex>
    <html:p>In the current Emacs preview this shows up as one long line of TeX-looking source with no formatting.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Inline markup.</html:strong> <html:code><![CDATA[\em{italic}]]></html:code>, <html:code><![CDATA[\strong{bold}]]></html:code>, and <html:code><![CDATA[\code{monospace}]]></html:code> all have visual distinction in the browser but currently flatten to indistinguishable runs of characters in the text preview.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Transclusion.</html:strong> A <html:code><![CDATA[\transclude{sss-XXXX}]]></html:code> call in the browser expands the target tree inline, often with its own math, code, and links. In the Emacs preview it shows as a literal <html:code><![CDATA[\transclude]]></html:code> call — the reader has to navigate away to see the content.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Datalog queries.</html:strong> Source like the <html:code>status-pending</html:code> query in <fr:link href="/forkester-features/" title="Features for Forking Forester" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/forkester-features/" display-uri="forkester-features" type="local">Features for Forking Forester</fr:link> produces a live list of trees in the browser but renders as a raw <html:code><![CDATA[\query\datalog{...}]]></html:code> block in Emacs with no results.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:strong>Links and cross-references.</html:strong> <html:code><![CDATA[[title](sss-XXXX)]]></html:code> is a clickable navigation in the browser; in the Emacs preview it's plain text with no indication that it's a link target.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
