                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>I am currently having Claude write a sketch of how to make a
handwritten notetaking app that I can self host, use with PencilKit,
and integrate with a rich, associative tagging system like Forester's.</html:p>
                    <html:p>Currently with the sketch of a Notability integration with
Forester, the tree is rendered with a thumbnail. Once this is
implemented, I would want to potentially render the handwritten note
in an in-browser canvas. I think HTML5 supports things like this. In
this way we can maybe have a read-only interactive view with the
handwritten note
</html:p>
                    <html:p>I've vibe coded a handwritten notes app for forester, but I am not
yet able to link a <html:code>pdf</html:code> to this forest, only <html:code>png</html:code>.</html:p>
