                  <fr:mainmatter>
                    <html:p>
  I often use my ipad pro to take handwritten notes, and I find it
  frustrating that digital handwritten notes don't interagte with my
  other knowledge management in Forester. I think that is a real point
  of frustration, as there is a significant cognitive friction
  managing two independent systems. So I often give up and just use
  one or none of them.
</html:p>
                    <html:p>
  We may wish to use OCR on notes as a hook when saving them, or
  perhaps as a nightly task. I don't know how effective that might be.
</html:p>
                    <html:p>
  Maybe something as simple as a capturing workflow where I can easily
  link to a digital handwritten note from within a normal tree. Then
  on each device we can register a program that opens a notetaking app
  of choice for handling handwritten notes. And maybe we can the
  ability to link to digital notes from handwritten ones as well, and
  the OCR could detect this?
</html:p>
                    <html:p>Merged into <fr:link href="/sss-0072/" title="ForesterPad: iPad App Redesign" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-0072/" display-uri="sss-0072" type="local">ForesterPad: iPad App Redesign</fr:link>.</html:p>
